WEBVTT

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:09.800
Nova Red online.

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:12.060
Starbase. Let's go.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:28.560
September twenty-eight, seven forty-eight Central time

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:31.880
Booster Twenty-One, Ship Forty-One, stacked in line

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:35.640
Thirty-three Raptor Threes light the Gulf on fire

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:38.980
Hot staging, six engines, climbing higher

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:42.360
One engine out, but the ship burns longer

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:45.660
Single Raptor relight, orbit, getting stronger

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:49.040
Flight Fourteen made it, first time in orbit

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:52.760
Twenty-six V3 Starlinks, she deployed it

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:53.580
Countdown, T minus ten

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.120
Flip, boostback, do it again

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:57.340
Gulf splashdown, termination test

00:00:58.060 --> 00:00:59.280
Booster did the mission, now the rest

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:06.020
Catch the ship, catch the ship, chopsticks open wide

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:09.300
Mechazilla arms, swinging side to side

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:12.680
Stainless steel, neon heat, burning through the night

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:16.180
Starbase, Starbase, bring it home tonight

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:19.520
Catch the ship, catch the ship, tower holding tight

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:21.960
Booster and the ship, a double catch in sight

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:26.280
Full reuse, close the loop, fly and fly again

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:29.880
Starbase, Starbase, count it down to ten

00:01:43.780 --> 00:01:45.620
Eighteen thousand tiles, hexagons of black

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:49.020
Silica ceramic, gotta make it back

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:52.360
Twenty-six hundred degrees on the way down

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:55.680
Heat shield holding, Pacific splashdown

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:59.420
Cameras on the Starlinks looking at the skin

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:02.280
Checking every tile to fly her again

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:06.140
Curved tiles in the gaps, plasma stopped cold

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:10.100
Two reflown tiles, the future's getting bold

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:11.380
Countdown, T minus ten

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:13.740
Flaps out, belly flop, then

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:15.860
Swing vertical, drop it in the rails

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:17.500
Engines light, the tower never fails

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:23.860
Catch the ship, catch the ship, chopsticks open wide

00:02:25.080 --> 00:02:27.140
Mechazilla arms, swinging side to side

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:30.480
Stainless steel, neon heat, burning through the night

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:33.920
Starbase, Starbase, bring it home tonight

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:37.280
Catch the ship, catch the ship, tower holding tight

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:39.700
Booster and the ship, a double catch in sight

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:43.880
Full reuse, close the loop, fly and fly again

00:02:43.900 --> 00:02:47.400
Starbase, Starbase, count it down to ten

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:50.280
Flight Five, Flight Seven, Flight Eight

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:53.960
Three booster catches, history made

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:56.940
October twenty twenty-four, the first time it was caught

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:00.680
Arms closed on the booster, more than we thought

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:04.120
Ship Forty-Two hung on the Pad Two arms

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:07.340
Practice catch in September, sounding the alarms

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:10.800
Flight Fifteen next, November's on the board

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:14.240
Not confirmed yet, but we're ready to roar

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.060
Booster Twenty-Two and Ship Forty-Two

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:17.720
Block Three stack, shiny and new

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:19.140
Catch both stages, that's the plan they said

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:21.000
First full recovery, if it goes ahead

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:22.680
More likely than not, that's the odds on the call

00:03:23.160 --> 00:03:24.380
Weekly flights next year, aiming for it all

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:26.060
Belly flop, flip, and a landing burn

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:27.940
Every single flight is a lesson to learn

